---
import PaletteTable from './PaletteTable.astro';
import { variants } from '../lib/palette';
---
<section class="palette-reference" id="palette" aria-labelledby="palette-title">
  <div class="section-panel">
    <header class="palette-head">
      <h2 id="palette-title">Palette reference</h2>
      <p>All three variants, with Hex, RGB, HSL, and OKLCH side by side.</p>
      <details class="palette-numbering">
        <summary>Colour names and numbering</summary>
        <p>Background colours run from <code>bg0</code> to <code>bg5</code>, and text colours from <code>fg5</code> to <code>fg0</code>. <code>bg0</code> is the darkest background in Coal and Smoulder, and the lightest in Ash.</p>
        <p>The examples are using <code>bg1</code> for backgrounds and <code>fg1</code> for body text but you can try any <code>fg</code>-<code>bg</code> combination.</p>
        <p>You can find each colour’s hex, RGB, HSL, OKLCH, and CSS names in the JSON file.</p>
      </details>
    </header>

{variants.map(variant => <PaletteTable variant={variant} />)}
</div>
</section>
